# His Name is Valgeir (otherAreas 3): its reply kinds against two Event-priority competitors set by a GM: Rycharde the
# Chef accepted (Rycharde 72, Take 68; RQ1 sorts before RQ4) and The Clue accepted (Rycharde 85, Take 65, Valgeir 143;
# RQ6 sorts after). On a tie the lookup's action cycle plays the actions in container order, one per talk, from where it
# last stopped. Available: Rycharde's 86 (Progress) twice; not due: 72, 75, 85 in turn (75 is Event); Take: 68, then 65
# (65 is not Progress; RQ4's 65 and The Clue's 65 share the id). Accepted, the pizza held: Rycharde 72, 87, 85 in turn;
# Felisa's 230 (Progress) over her script twice (an Event 230 would alternate with her script: the second talk would be
# 221). Selbina: Valgeir's 100 (Progress) twice (the pizza given back by a GM), then without it 101 (Event) and 143 in
# turn. Mhaura: Rycharde's 88 (Progress: an Event 88 would have tied and the cycle would play 72).
